{
  "slug": "loop-and-gate-foundation",
  "name": "Loop And Gate Foundation",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A self-improving agent loop with plain-text Obsidian memory. Skills for capture, reflect, and improve; a SessionStart hook injects working memory each session. The teaching-tier Foundation of the Loop & Gate stack.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **10 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (10): `add-kits` (Offer to install the rest of the Loop & Gate stack — the Build, Grow, and Accountability kits,…), `capture` (Save durable knowledge to the vault), `improve` (Apply accumulated self-improvement signals), `inbox-triage` (Process raw thoughts captured elsewhere (phone at a red light, Obsidian mobile) that landed in vault/Inbox/), `loop` (Orchestrate a goal through subagent iterations), `profile-interview` (Bootstrap the user's voice profile and taste profile by interviewing them, one question at a time), `reflect` (Close out an agent session), `session-start` (Load working memory at the start of every agent session), and 2 more\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install loop-and-gate-foundation@claude-community` from `slogsdon/loop-and-gate-foundation`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 10,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
